  "notes": "FALL START ONLY. Catalog prints 60-61 credit hours. Term I offers EMER 1006 (6 cr) OR EMER 1007 (7 cr); Term II offers EMER 1007 OR EMER 2007 Advanced EMT (7 cr). Recorded configuration (61 hrs): EMER 1007 in Term I, EMER 2007 in Term II (the Advanced EMT path; CP in Advanced EMT embedded in Term II). The EMER 1006 (Emergency Medical Responder) path totals 60 credit hours. Special admissions requirements apply to EMER 1007, EMER 2007, and PHLB 1016 (age 18, HS diploma/equivalent, GPA 2.0, program application, substance abuse screening, background check, TB test; EMER 2007 requires EMER 1007 with current NREMT license before clinicals). Catalog note: 'Real World Math is the recommended math course for this degree. College Algebra may also be taken to satisfy this requirement.' Transfer: Arkansas State University BS Disaster Preparedness and Emergency Management; BAS Organizational Supervision (full junior classification).",
